WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.334
-Enjoy yourself.
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.300
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:09.033
Very special,
very special episode.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:10.601
You guys, I'm excited about
this.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:14.667
Yankees superstar Aaron Judge is
on the show tonight!

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:17.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:19.968
We love Aaron Judge.
Of course, Aaron is so kind.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.634
Backstage I asked for a selfie,

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:23.501
and he was nice enough to pick
me up for the photo.

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:25.434
-Aww.
-I thought that was cool.

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:28.033
Last season, Aaron hit
62 home runs,

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.734
surpassing players like
Roger Maris and Babe Ruth.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.367
And here's a fun stat.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.501
Between the three men,
Biden's met them all.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.234
Let's get to some news here.

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.701
On Friday, the FBI spent
13 hours searching

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:43.267
President Biden's house
in Wilmington, Delaware,

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:46.267
and they found more
classified documents.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.400
You know what?
At this point, just let us know

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.234
when you stop finding them.
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.634
Meanwhile, as if the documents
weren't crazy enough, they also

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.767
found the script for the last
season of "Stranger Things."

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:59.601
Ooh.
How is he getting all this?

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:02.367
The Justice Department also took
handwritten notes

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.267
from when Biden was
vice president.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.767
One was a piece of paper
addressed to Obama that just

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:09.367
said, "Do you like me?
Check yes or no."

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:13.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.334
-Wow.
-It's crazy.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:16.801
First Trump, now Biden.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:19.434
Today, just to be safe, Obama
burned his house down.

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:21.734
He's like --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.934
It's interesting how Biden
and Trump have handled

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:25.367
their situations differently.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:28.300
Biden has new documents found
every week, while Trump went for

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.367
the Netflix style --
binge all at once release.

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:32.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:33.767
Yeah, it's not a good look for
Biden.

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:36.901
And now even top Democrats are
criticizing him for his handling

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:40.334
of classified documents, calling
him irresponsible and saying

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:41.868
that he should be embarrassed.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.767
Yeah, they're really piling on.

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.767
Here, check out what some other
Democrats had to say.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.634
First up, Senator Cory Booker
said...

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.634
Then Senator John Fetterman
said...

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.601
And Senator Bernie Sanders
said...

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.200
And Senator Jon Tester said...

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:19.267
Senator Tom Carper said...

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:28.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.033
And Senator Joe Manchin said...

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:38.667
So Senator Jon Ossoff said...

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:47.400
And finally, Senator Cory Booker
said...

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:51.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.167
Everyone's got something to say.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:59.400
Some more news from Washington.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.567
This weekend the news broke that
Biden's chief of staff

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.834
Ron Klain is stepping down.

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:07.334
Yep. Klain said, "Look, I hate
leaving you with such a mess,

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:08.601
but I will anyway."

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:11.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.868
Of course, being Biden's chief
of staff is a tough job.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:17.167
You have to be able to write
and speak in size 72 font.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:21.934
"Your tie is croo--
Oh, forget it."

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.000
At first it was unclear
who was stepping down

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.534
because Biden calls everyone
chief.

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:28.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.100
"Hey, chief."

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.133
Well, get this.
TikTok just confirmed that some

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:35.968
of its employees have the power
to decide which videos go viral.

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:37.968
[ Audience oohs ]
Yeah, it's crazy.

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:39.968
So, basically employees
make the decision

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.567
that this should not go viral.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.400
-So, one thing that people have
asked if I've tried

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.934
quite a lot is boba.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:48.300
-But this should go viral.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.434
-Poke a hole in it.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:57.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:00.234
-What?
-Here's another example.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:02.734
Employees decided that this
should not go viral.

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:03.868
-Whoo!

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.801
[ Audience ohs ]

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:09.334
-But this should.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:11.501
-Us teachers would never ask you
students

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:14.501
to do anything we wouldn't do
ourselves.

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:17.567
[ Groans ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:21.634
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:21.634 --> 00:04:25.701
-Wow. Wow.
-Wow.

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:28.434
-That's right. They didn't think
that this should go viral.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:34.300
But they thought that this
should.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.534
-And his name is John Cena!

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:43.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:46.601
-And finally, they decided this
should not go viral.

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:51.067
But this should.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.534
[ Audience oohs ]
[ Applause ]

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:57.200
Interesting choices.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:00.300
We would never do --

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:05.667
Switching gears,
Buckingham Palace has revealed

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:09.067
the details of King Charles'
coronation, which will include

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:11.067
three days of celebrations.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:13.601
I just hope all this partying
doesn't leave him too exhausted

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:15.234
to not do any work the next day.

00:05:15.234 --> 00:05:19.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.701
I also saw that the coronation

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.467
will also break away
from tradition.

00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:25.534
Yeah, apparently when Charles
steps onto the palace balcony,

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:27.234
he's going to toss Mardi Gras
beads.

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:29.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:30.601
Well, people are talking about
this.

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:33.267
On Saturday at a resort in
Dubai, Beyoncé performed

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:35.801
her first full concert
in four years

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:39.767
and was reportedly paid $24
million for the hour-long show.

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.534
[ Audience oohs ]

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:44.067
$24 million for a one-hour
performance.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:47.634
Even Aaron Judge was like,
"Damn, that is a lot of money!"

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:50.300
Hey, this is exciting.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:53.200
Tomorrow the Oscar nominations
will be announced.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.601
And yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.601 --> 00:05:58.801
And apparently, "Top Gun:
Maverick" is expected to be

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:01.767
nominated for Best Picture,
marking the first time in

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:04.133
a decade people have said,
"Oh, my God, I've seen one."

00:06:04.133 --> 00:06:07.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.567
Some more entertainment news --

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.868
the new season of "The Bachelor"
kicks off tonight.

00:06:10.868 --> 00:06:13.200
[ Cheering ]

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.634
It's actually the most shocking
season ever because they find

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:18.434
classified documents
in the fantasy suite.

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:19.968
[ Laughter ]
I don't know.

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:21.968
That's what I'm hearing.

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:24.000
Well, listen to this.
The president of Ireland has

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.467
called on schools to stop giving
homework so kids can use

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:30.367
their free time for other
creative things.

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:31.734
-Ooh.

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:33.734
-That story again --
the president of Ireland is

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:35.367
apparently my 9-year-old
daughter.

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:36.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:39.200
Candy for dinner!

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.667
Did you guys see this?

00:06:40.667 --> 00:06:43.334
I read that the world's worst
McDonald's, which police were

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:45.868
called to more than 800 times
in one year,

00:06:45.868 --> 00:06:48.033
is permanently closing.

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:50.033
On the bright side, they just
changed the sign,

00:06:50.033 --> 00:06:51.968
and now it's the world's best
Waffle House.

00:06:51.968 --> 00:06:54.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.033 --> 00:06:58.701
[ Applause ]

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:00.367
And finally,
have you guys noticed

00:07:00.367 --> 00:07:02.234
that when you start
typing something on Google,

00:07:02.234 --> 00:07:04.868
it automatically tries to
complete the search for you?

00:07:04.868 --> 00:07:07.234
It autofills
what you're looking for?

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:08.901
Sometimes their suggestions
are a little off.

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:11.567
I'll show you what I mean.
It's time for Google Autofails.

00:07:11.567 --> 00:07:15.334
-♪ Google autofails ♪

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:16.834
♪ Yeah ♪

00:07:16.834 --> 00:07:18.834
-Just look at what I did today.

00:07:18.834 --> 00:07:21.100
I typed in
"How did Yellowstone..."

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.133
and these three things
popped up.

00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:24.868
"season 4 end?"

00:07:24.868 --> 00:07:26.734
"get so popular?"

00:07:26.734 --> 00:07:28.033
"convince my dad
to start dressing

00:07:28.033 --> 00:07:29.400
like Woody from Toy Story?"

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.968
He works in an office!

00:07:32.968 --> 00:07:34.601
Here's another one.

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:36.434
I typed in
"Why is Joe Burrow..."

00:07:36.434 --> 00:07:39.033
It said "so good,"

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:40.567
"number 9,"

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:41.801
"in my wife's search history?"

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:43.934
[ Applause ]

00:07:43.934 --> 00:07:46.834
-Wait, what?

00:07:46.834 --> 00:07:48.067
-Next up, I typed in,

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:50.400
"How to return" and it said,

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.934
"a package to Amazon,"

00:07:51.934 --> 00:07:53.467
"cable equipment to Spectrum,"

00:07:53.467 --> 00:07:55.501
"Prince Harry to England."

00:07:55.501 --> 00:07:57.434
[ Applause ]

00:07:57.434 --> 00:07:59.934
They --

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:01.734
-That's not you.
That's an autofill.

00:08:01.734 --> 00:08:03.467
-After that, I typed in,

00:08:03.467 --> 00:08:05.868
"Why can't I sleep?"
and it said,

00:08:05.868 --> 00:08:07.200
"through the night,"

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.634
"on my back,"

00:08:08.634 --> 00:08:11.167
"without scrolling through
TikTok for three hours first?"

00:08:11.167 --> 00:08:13.133
"I'll just check it,
just real quick.

00:08:13.133 --> 00:08:15.834
I'll just --" Pretty good.

00:08:15.834 --> 00:08:18.367
Next up, I typed in
"Whatever happened to..."

00:08:18.367 --> 00:08:20.267
it said "Amelia Earhart,"

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:21.701
"Susan Boyle,"

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:25.767
"Predictability? The milkman,
the paperboy, evening TV."

00:08:25.767 --> 00:08:29.234
[ Applause ]

00:08:29.234 --> 00:08:30.767
After that, I typed in

00:08:30.767 --> 00:08:32.067
"How to survive..."

00:08:32.067 --> 00:08:33.667
It said "a tornado,"

00:08:33.667 --> 00:08:35.067
"a hurricane,"

00:08:35.067 --> 00:08:37.734
"a fight in the bathroom
with Marjorie Taylor Greene?"

00:08:37.734 --> 00:08:39.167
[ Applause ]

00:08:39.167 --> 00:08:41.968
I don't know.
How do you do it?

00:08:41.968 --> 00:08:43.200
Next up, I typed in

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.434
"Why do the Girl Scouts..."
and it said,

00:08:45.434 --> 00:08:47.267
"sell cookies?"

00:08:47.267 --> 00:08:48.467
"wear sashes?"

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:50.167
"guard the entrance
to the grocery store

00:08:50.167 --> 00:08:51.601
like they're
the National Guard?"

00:08:51.601 --> 00:08:53.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:53.033 --> 00:08:54.601
You going somewhere?

00:08:54.601 --> 00:08:58.234
[ Applause ]

00:08:58.234 --> 00:08:59.434
And finally, I typed in,

00:08:59.434 --> 00:09:00.801
"Am I the only one without..."

00:09:00.801 --> 00:09:02.467
and it said, "a 401k?"

00:09:02.467 --> 00:09:04.167
"a car?"

00:09:04.167 --> 00:09:06.000
"classified documents
in my garage?"

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.133
That's all for Google Autofails.

